    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 offensive outlook for May 22, 2026, centers on **Gunnar Henderson**, whose 83.29 efficiency score makes him our clear anchor. A favorable park factor (+16%) and a strong dynamic platoon edge against a hittable arm yield the day's highest ceiling. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (72.21) and **Josh Jung** (66.18) follow as critical pillars; **Josh Jung** in particular benefits from a soft matchup against Grayson Rodriguez (5.91 xERA), with the optimizer leaning heavily into that elite SP-skill delta. Meanwhile, **Nasim Nunez** remains a tactical inclusion despite the lower score (54.47); his speed profile makes him an indispensable asset in our 5x5 build, and his ability to exploit slow pitcher deliveries keeps him ahead of players with higher raw batting projections.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Nolan Schanuel** (44.77). He was the final cut, narrowly missing the cut-off due to the sheer dominance of Jacob deGrom\u2019s profile; even with a decent order spot, the suppressed floor against an elite arm made him a safer hold than starting him over the likes of **Dominic Smith** or **Gage Workman**, whose matchups against lower-tier lefties provide better efficiency. We continue to monitor the statuses of **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** on the IL, as their absence remains a significant drag on our potential output in SB and HR categories. With no major weather concerns reported, the primary risk remains the high SP-skill variance against starters like McDonald and Henderson, who are projected to suppress scoring across our OF slots.",
